`,s.jsx(v,{items:[{q:"State Dice in terms of TP, FP and FN, and say what other metric that makes it.",a:"Dice = 2TP / (2TP + FP + FN), which is exactly the F1 score computed over pixels — the harmonic mean of precision and recall. IoU is TP / (TP + FP + FN); the only difference is that Dice counts the intersection twice, once in each mask's area, which is why it always reads higher."},{q:"A paper reports Dice 0.92 and another reports IoU 0.92. Which is better, and by how much?",a:"The IoU one, substantially. Dice 0.92 corresponds to IoU = D/(2−D) = 0.852, whereas IoU 0.92 corresponds to Dice 0.958. They are monotone in each other so they never disagree about ranking, but the numbers are on different scales and quoting them side by side is misleading."}]}),`
